Extract the scalars, substitute the given ordered products, and add corresponding components:

$$
\begin{aligned}
&=-4(\mathbf{a}\times \mathbf{c})-6(\mathbf{b}\times \mathbf{c}) \\ &=-4(\langle 0,-2,-2\rangle)-6(\langle 0,-3,1\rangle) \\ &=(\langle 0,8,8\rangle)+(\langle 0,18,-6\rangle) \\ &=\langle 0,26,2\rangle
